# (after 0506) nvn/present: a texture the game presents keeps its stores; every present classified (drawn / not written / never
# written / Metal texture replaced) and counted
#
# Why: South Park: The Fractured But Whole (01008F2005154000) on an iPhone 15 Pro (A17 Pro): during loading the previous picture stays, then the screen alternates image /
#   black for about 2 s (owner, 2026-11-21). The device log has loading frames presented with @draws=0 in which 4 loaded 1280x720 RGBA8 attachments (the window textures'
#   size and format) were stored DontCare (@unwritten_dc_mb=14.06). On the console a texture is its memory, so presenting without drawing shows the old picture. Here a pass
#   that loads an attachment and writes nothing stores DontCare (udc_on, DM_NVN_UNWRITTEN_DC), which Metal defines as undefined contents; the engine checked that rule on
#   an A19 Pro and Macs, not on an A17 Pro.
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m, hle_nvn.c; a test):
#   * sd_finish: a colour attachment whose texture the game has presented (the last 4 presented textures, by serial) keeps MTLStoreActionStore when it was loaded and not
#     written. Every other attachment follows the DontCare rule as before, and the mandatory image-only rule is untouched. Cost: one window-texture store per such pass.
#     DM_NVN_PRESENT_KEEP=0 restores the old behaviour.
#   * ps_note_present (present_enqueue, submit thread). Each present is classified:
#     - drawn, cleared or copied into since its previous present;
#     - not written since (the console shows its old bytes);
#     - never written since the host made it (the host shows zeros, the console its storage);
#     - shown through another Metal texture than last time (content lost: "[RED] ... what was drawn into it before is gone").
#     First cases and powers of two are logged, with a "presented textures up to present N" summary per window texture every 300 presents. That summary gives presents,
#     drawn, not written, never written, replaced, in frames with no draw, and stores kept.
#     mtl_present_unwritten() feeds the slow-frame row @pres_unwritten (weak reference in hle_nvn.c).
#   * Writes counted: draws and clears into a colour attachment, OP_COPY_B2T / OP_COPY_T2T / OP_CLEAR_TEX into it. NOT counted: compute image stores, so a window texture
#     written by a compute shader shows as "not written".
# DEFAULT: keep on, census always on (a 4-entry table per pass end and per present).
# What a device log then tells:
#   - "not written" presents in frames with no draw and no more black: the DontCare loss was it (the keep is the fix);
#   - "replaced" / "never written" lines at the flashes: the host lost the texture, not the store (a sharing-table / texture lifetime problem; DM_NVN_PRESENT_KEEP does not cure that);
#   - every present "drawn" while black frames are seen: the game's own draws come out black (draws skipped: draft 0506's counts; or inputs read as dummies).
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad).
# Test: dm/gfx/tests/t_present_keep (10 checks with the keep on and 10 with DM_NVN_PRESENT_KEEP=0; make check_t_present_keep). Rebuilt with 0506 + 0507 on an M1 Pro:
#   t_dead_targets 197/0, t_nvn 506/0, t_addr_known 14/0, t_pool_chunks 178/0, t_vbuf_clamp 15/0 + 13/0. NOT run on a device; no host dylib built.

# Rebased 2026-11-22 onto the new 0506 (upstream c96c45e9 + 79555b67 + the pool-end fallback): context only, same behaviour.

